  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ NOW US-Inequality Disruptors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a result of social cultural practices such as patriarchy, women in the lake zone region, particularly in Mwanza, are often regarded as individuals of a lower class and are perceived as someone whose primary responsibilities are to care for the family and bear children. While the vast majority of the men folk are engaged in either smallscale agricultural practices, business, or employment. The household chores of the women take up the majority of their time, and they are not given a voice in the decisions that affect their families. They are also prevented from obtaining a higher education and are wholly reliant on their male counterparts. In addition, they are forced to take the burden of the majority of social ills, such as dowry systems and domesticabuse. The majority of the women in the Isamilo ward of Mwanza are actively engaging in unpaid work. As a result, the majority of the activities these women participate in are for subsistence purposes rather than activities that result in income. This contributes to a cycle of poverty amongwomen in the lake zone and an increased gap of inequality, particularly with regard to access to and ownership of productive resources. Now Us Cooperative has the intention of putting into action a project that will raise awareness about women&apos;s rights to employment and access to productive resources such as land and properties. The goal of this project is to make a long-term improvement in the quality of life of women who are socially marginalized. Our effort will begin by organizing and forming three self-saving groups inside the Isamilo ward. Each of these groups should have ten different women participating. After that, we will offer training on leadership skills and financial literacy. This training should encompass the process of saving money and skills for managing finances. At the meeting of the villagers, we will organize and lead a session to raise awareness and sensitization about women&apos;s rights to access to employment and their contribution to the growth ofthe economy at the home level. We will organize a group meeting and approach financial institutions, local government agencies (LGAs), and other interested partners about supporting the three groups with seed capital that will be repaid without interest.One example of a stakeholder that we will engage with is an Islamic bank, which isone type of lender that does not charge interest on loans. In addition, we have plans to provide mentoring and coaching services towomen in order to ensure that they aresuccessful in running their existing businesses, which will allow them to pay back the loans they have received and carry on with their other revenue-generating endeavours.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="XM-DAC-7" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs NL</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Now Us Cooperative Society began as a group of seven young and dynamic women in 2018 with the intention of not just economically empowering one another, but also aiding other young women with knowledge about financial literacy, life skills, sexual reproductive health rights, and confidence building. After a number of years of operation, Now Us cooperative society came to the realization that our group has a significant impact in the community community. This was brought to attention by the fact that morewomen were interested in joining the group, and that local leaders began inviting us to community meetings in order for Now Us cooperative society to share knowledge regarding financial resiliency with groups that receive loans at the district level.  in2020 we were required by lawto be registered as a community-based organization with the registration number
MCC/CD/SHG/530,  the Now us Cooperative Society constitution, consist of 11recognized members, whereby one is a chairperson, other is secretary and treasurer. The primary objective ofthe Now Us cooperative society is to provide assistance to women and young girls who are confronted with a
variety of challenges inour communities, such as being a victim of domestic violence, having a child at a young age, being a widow, and other similar circumstances, which prevent them from fully participating in economic activity, achieving financial independence, and making a contribution to the economic well-being of their families. Our group was established,among other things, to give education about sexual reproductive health rights, financial literacy, and entrepreneurialism; to establish a village community-saving system, and to launch minor income-generating activities to fund our
organization&apos;s ongoingoperations</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Now Us Cooperative Society</narrative>
